WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:06.560
Eruptions from a volcano on the Spanish island of&nbsp;
La Palma have intensified, with a new vent opening&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:13.360
up, releasing more lava. More than 400 homes have&nbsp;
been destroyed so far. Ash and dust from the new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:18.080
fissure have forced the island's authorities&nbsp;
to ground air travel until further notice.&nbsp;

00:00:21.920 --> 00:00:27.840
The fiery cauldron of Cumbre Vieja,&nbsp;
spewing livid magma and clouds of ash.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:33.280
A week of eruptions has created a cone&nbsp;
more than one hundred meters high,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.280 --> 00:00:38.960
which is now beginning to collapse under&nbsp;
its own weight, unleashing a river of lava.&nbsp;

00:00:42.160 --> 00:00:46.880
Residents of La Palma can only watch&nbsp;
and wonder what will come next.&nbsp;

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:52.720
"I am very, very worried about the situation&nbsp;
of the ash, because the ash is blanketing the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.720 --> 00:00:58.160
neighborhood. It's been a disaster for all&nbsp;
the plants, animals and all the buildings."&nbsp;

00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:06.720
A new vent opened over the weekend. It's&nbsp;
feared more homes may be swallowed by lava.&nbsp;

00:01:07.600 --> 00:01:10.240
Already hundreds of properties&nbsp;
have been destroyed.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:10.880 --> 00:01:15.520
Those evacuated days ago still&nbsp;
cannot return to retrieve belongings.&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.600
The island's banana plantations&nbsp;
are also under threat.&nbsp;

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:25.680
Airport workers clear a&nbsp;
blanket of ash from the runway,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:25.680 --> 00:01:30.640
though all flights have been suspended.
Tourists are evacuating by sea,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.200 --> 00:01:36.160
abandoning their holidays, and sparing a&nbsp;
thought for the locals who must stay behind.&nbsp;

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:40.400
"I feel sad for the people&nbsp;
here who are struggling.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:45.440
We didn't enjoy it the way we should have.&nbsp;
We feel very bad about what is happening."&nbsp;

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:53.040
Scientists say they can't predict how the&nbsp;
lava will flow. The Spanish government plans&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:53.040 --> 00:02:07.840
to soon designate the island a disaster zone&nbsp;
- making official what is already visible.

